{"id":"ecea5dcf-6c37-4ada-928b-4c210476db25","object":"chat.completion","created":1785036534,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    word_token_indices = case['word_token_indices']\\n    word_scores = case['word_scores']\\n    forced_words = case['forced_words']\\n    token_budget = case['token_budget']\\n    n = len(word_token_indices)\\n    best_mask = None\\n    best_score = -1.0\\n    best_tokens = set()\\n    for mask in range(1 << n):\\n        include = True\\n        for fw in forced_words:\\n            if not (mask >> fw) & 1:\\n                include = False\\n                break\\n        if not include:\\n            continue\\n        tokens = set()\\n        score = 0.0\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if (mask >> i) & 1:\\n                tokens.update(word_token_indices[i])\\n                score += word_scores[i]\\n        if len(tokens) > token_budget:\\n            continue\\n        if score > best_score:\\n            best_score = score\\n            best_mask = mask\\n            best_tokens = tokens\\n    if best_mask is None:\\n        mask = 0\\n        for fw in forced_words:\\n            mask |= (1 << fw)\\n        tokens = set()\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if (mask >> i) & 1:\\n                tokens.update(word_token_indices[i])\\n        best_mask = mask\\n        best_tokens = tokens\\n    selected_words = [i for i in range(n) if (best_mask >> i) & 1]\\n    retained_token_indices = sorted(best_tokens)\\n    tokens_used = len(retained_token_indices)\\n    return {\\n        'retained_token_indices': retained_token_indices,\\n        'selected_words': selected_words,\\n        'tokens_used': tokens_used\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write solve(case) for task NLP-LL2-02. The case payload has fields: word_token_indices (list of lists of token indices per word), word_scores (list of floats, same length as word_token_indices), forced_words (list of word indices that must be selected), token_budget (integer maximum total tokens that can be selected). The task is to select a subset of words (where each word is a set of token indices) such that the total number of distinct tokens selected (union of tokens) does not exceed token_budget, and we must include all forced_words. The goal is to maximize the sum of word_scores of selected words. This is a classic knapsack-like problem with union constraint, NP-hard. But given small sizes (likely small number of words and tokens), we can brute force using bitmask over words (if number of words <= ~20) or use DP over tokens? Token indices can be large (like up to maybe 100? but the fixture shows small). It says use only standard library, no numpy. We need to return retained_token_indices (list of token indices that are selected, presumably the union of tokens from selected words), selected_words (list of word indices selected), tokens_used (integer count of distinct tokens). The output schema: retained_token_indices is list of integers, selected_words list of integers, tokens_used integer.\n\nWe have to implement solve(case) that returns this dict.\n\nWe need to choose which words to select to maximize sum scores given token budget and forced words. The problem is a maximum coverage / subset selection with a cardinality constraint on tokens. Since the number of words is likely small (fixture shows 6 words), we can enumerate all subsets of words that include forced words, check token count, and pick best. Use bitmask from 0 to (1<<n)-1. For each mask, check if all forced words are set. Then compute union of token indices from selected words; count distinct tokens; if <= budget, compute sum scores; keep best.\n\nEdge cases: if forced words alone exceed budget? Then no feasible solution? But perhaps forced words must be selected anyway; we should include them even if over budget? The problem statement says \"we must include all forced_words\". If token budget is too small, perhaps we still select them and tokens_used > budget? The task likely expects we respect budget and exclude forced words if impossible? But likely budget is always sufficient. We'll assume forced words are included and if budget insufficient, we still include them (as required) and tokens_used may exceed budget. But to be safe, we can follow typical logic: forced words must be selected; if their tokens exceed budget, we still select them (since required). The output should reflect actual tokens used.\n\nWe'll implement solve(case) as described.\n\nWe'll encode as Python source inside JSON implementation string.\n\nNeed to escape newlines and quotes.\n\nWrite code:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    word_token_indices = case['word_token_indices']\n    word_scores = case['word_scores']\n    forced_words = case['forced_words']\n    token_budget = case['token_budget']\n    n = len(word_token_indices)\n    best_mask = None\n    best_score = -1.0\n    best_tokens = set()\n    for mask in range(1 << n):\n        # check forced words included\n        include = True\n        for fw in forced_words:\n            if not (mask >> fw) & 1:\n                include = False\n                break\n        if not include:\n            continue\n        # compute tokens\n        tokens = set()\n        score = 0.0\n        for i in range(n):\n            if (mask >> i) & 1:\n                tokens.update(word_token_indices[i])\n                score += word_scores[i]\n        if len(tokens) > token_budget:\n            continue\n        if score > best_score:\n            best_score = score\n            best_mask = mask\n            best_tokens = tokens\n    # if no feasible set, fallback: select only forced words (even if over budget)\n    if best_mask is None:\n        # include all forced words\n        mask = 0\n        for fw in forced_words:\n            mask |= (1 << fw)\n        tokens = set()\n        for i in range(n):\n            if (mask >> i) & 1:\n                tokens.update(word_token_indices[i])\n        best_mask = mask\n        best_tokens = tokens\n    selected_words = [i for i in range(n) if (best_mask >> i) & 1]\n    retained_token_indices = sorted(best_tokens)\n    tokens_used = len(retained_token_indices)\n    return {\n        'retained_token_indices': retained_token_indices,\n        'selected_words': selected_words,\n        'tokens_used': tokens_used\n    }\n\nThat's it.\n\nNow, produce JSON with key \"implementation\" containing this code as a string, escaped properly.\n\nWe'll write the code with proper indentation, then escape.\n\nWe need to ensure no trailing spaces etc.\n\nLet's construct the JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1187,"completion_tokens":1514,"total_tokens":2701,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1152},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1082},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1152,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":35},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}